#!/usr/bin/env ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

require "optparse"
require "yard_md"

parser = OptionParser.new(<<~HELP)
  Reads the documentation yard-md wrote for a project's gems, by constant.

  Usage: mdri <Constant>[#method|.method] [output dir]

  Run in a project. Reads the documentation yard-md wrote into <output dir>
  for the gems its bundle resolves on this platform, at those versions:

    mdri Faraday                           its documentation, then its constants,
                                           classes, modules and methods
    mdri Faraday::Connection#run_request   that instance method's documentation
    mdri Faraday.new                       that class method's documentation
    mdri Faraday::VERSION                  that constant's value and documentation

  Each line of a list says what lies behind it: a constant's value, or its
  size when longer than a line of 80 characters; a class's or module's kind
  and how many constants, modules, classes and methods it holds; a method's
  summary. A class or module with nothing to list answers with its kind and
  the gems it is in.

  Every gem in the bundle answers, so a namespace several gems add to lists
  them all, and a class a gem reopens, such as String, answers for that gem.

  The output directory defaults to gem-docs/ in XDG_CACHE_HOME, or in ~/.cache
  when that is unset, empty or relative: here, #{YardMd::CACHE}.

  Prints the answer and writes nothing. When nothing in the bundle documents
  what it is asked, says so on stderr and exits non-zero. A gem answers once
  yard-md has documented it; one documented by yard-md 0.1.0 answers after
  yard-md --force documents it again.

  Options: -h, --help shows this; -v, --version prints the version.
HELP
parser.version = YardMd::VERSION

trap("INT") { exit 130 }

begin
  address, *output = parser.parse(ARGV)
  abort parser.help unless address && output.size <= 1
  answer = YardMd::Bundle.new(*output).read(address)
  abort "mdri: nothing in the bundle documents #{address}" unless answer
  print answer
rescue OptionParser::ParseError, YardMd::Error, SystemCallError
  parser.abort
end
